  '3bb2fae1-66bd-2442-8afe-bdb5e23e356c', 'b7cf29c6-2d92-41e1-b754-0035bddf8d6e', N'AAC.5.b: Objective Element B. Objective element b for AAC.5 requirement.', N'Within chapter Access Assessment and Continuity of Care (AAC), objective element AAC.5.b (title: Objective Element B) is a measurable checkpoint under parent requirement AAC.5. It implements: Patients cared for by the organisation undergo a regular re-assessment.. Meeting this OE demonstrates structured practice for NABH 6th Edition in this domain, reduces patient-safety and operational risk in Front Office / Clinical, and provides assessable evidence for survey.', N'1) Assign accountability: Admission In-charge with Front Office / Clinical participation. 2) Align SOPs/work instructions to AAC.5.b and the intent of AAC.5. 3) Train and competency-check staff; retain records. 4) Run monitoring (audits, KPIs, committee review) for scope As Applicable. 5) Collect evidence per Document expectations. 6) Track NC/CAPA to closure with evidence.', N'For AAC.5.b under AAC.5, maintain retrievable evidence suitable for Document review: controlled policies/procedures; approvals; registers; completed forms; patient/staff records; meeting minutes; improvement plans. Also retain metadata for traceability (version, author, date). NABH 6th Edition surveys may use structured evidence including app-based or photographic artefacts where the methodology permits.', N'OE AAC.5.b (Objective Element B) - parent AAC.5
- Mapped to chapter AAC: Access Assessment and Continuity of Care (AAC).
- Owner: Admission In-charge; departments: Front Office / Clinical.
- Current policy/SOP and training records available.
- Operational records / sampling for As Applicable.
- Evidence pack for Document ready.
- KPIs/committees reviewed; NC/CAPA closed with evidence.', N'Medium', N'High', N'NABH;6E;AAC;OE;AAC.5.b;Document;AAC.5', 1, 1);
