  '9589046a-c7d4-694e-a5c9-7d4daf9a0a55', '91ed0020-6470-4a7f-84ba-17aee9e001a9', N'PSQ.5.a: Objective Element A. Objective element a for PSQ.5 requirement.', N'Within chapter Patient Safety and Quality Improvement (PSQ), objective element PSQ.5.a (title: Objective Element A) is a measurable checkpoint under parent requirement PSQ.5. It implements: There is an established system for clinical audit.. Meeting this OE demonstrates structured practice for NABH 6th Edition in this domain, reduces patient-safety and operational risk in Quality Management, and provides assessable evidence for survey.', N'1) Assign accountability: Quality Head with Quality Management participation. 2) Align SOPs/work instructions to PSQ.5.a and the intent of PSQ.5. 3) Train and competency-check staff; retain records. 4) Run monitoring (audits, KPIs, committee review) for scope As Applicable. 5) Collect evidence per Document expectations. 6) Track NC/CAPA to closure with evidence.', N'For PSQ.5.a under PSQ.5, maintain retrievable evidence suitable for Document review: controlled policies/procedures; approvals; registers; completed forms; patient/staff records; meeting minutes; improvement plans. Also retain metadata for traceability (version, author, date). NABH 6th Edition surveys may use structured evidence including app-based or photographic artefacts where the methodology permits.', N'OE PSQ.5.a (Objective Element A) - parent PSQ.5
- Mapped to chapter PSQ: Patient Safety and Quality Improvement (PSQ).
- Owner: Quality Head; departments: Quality Management.
- Current policy/SOP and training records available.
- Operational records / sampling for As Applicable.
- Evidence pack for Document ready.
- KPIs/committees reviewed; NC/CAPA closed with evidence.', N'Low', N'Medium', N'NABH;6E;PSQ;OE;PSQ.5.a;Document;PSQ.5', 1, 1);
