  '745b212e-4ff7-9141-944f-9b86e6b688d3', '5f2171df-d0be-4c89-ba13-41355040c8d9', N'FMS.2.f: Objective Element F. Objective element f for FMS.2 requirement.', N'Within chapter Facility Management and Safety (FMS), objective element FMS.2.f (title: Objective Element F) is a measurable checkpoint under parent requirement FMS.2. It implements: The organisation’s environment and facilities operate in a planned manner and promotes environment-friendly measures.. Meeting this OE demonstrates structured practice for NABH 6th Edition in this domain, reduces patient-safety and operational risk in Facility / Engineering, and provides assessable evidence for survey.', N'1) Assign accountability: Facility Manager with Facility / Engineering participation. 2) Align SOPs/work instructions to FMS.2.f and the intent of FMS.2. 3) Train and competency-check staff; retain records. 4) Run monitoring (audits, KPIs, committee review) for scope As Applicable. 5) Collect evidence per Document expectations. 6) Track NC/CAPA to closure with evidence.', N'For FMS.2.f under FMS.2, maintain retrievable evidence suitable for Document review: controlled policies/procedures; approvals; registers; completed forms; patient/staff records; meeting minutes; improvement plans. Also retain metadata for traceability (version, author, date). NABH 6th Edition surveys may use structured evidence including app-based or photographic artefacts where the methodology permits.', N'OE FMS.2.f (Objective Element F) - parent FMS.2
- Mapped to chapter FMS: Facility Management and Safety (FMS).
- Owner: Facility Manager; departments: Facility / Engineering.
- Current policy/SOP and training records available.
- Operational records / sampling for As Applicable.
- Evidence pack for Document ready.
- KPIs/committees reviewed; NC/CAPA closed with evidence.', N'Medium', N'High', N'NABH;6E;FMS;OE;FMS.2.f;Document;FMS.2', 1, 1);
