  '380dffbf-796f-714b-81f7-0364f66cf80a', 'aceea2d2-b874-4acd-bcad-49a96cac3d16', N'PRE.3.b: Objective Element B. Objective element b for PRE.3 requirement.', N'Within chapter Patient Rights and Education (PRE), objective element PRE.3.b (title: Objective Element B) is a measurable checkpoint under parent requirement PRE.3. It implements: The patient and / or family members are educated to make informed decisions and are involved in the care planning and delivery process.. Meeting this OE demonstrates structured practice for NABH 6th Edition in this domain, reduces patient-safety and operational risk in Quality / Patient Relations, and provides assessable evidence for survey.', N'1) Assign accountability: Quality Manager with Quality / Patient Relations participation. 2) Align SOPs/work instructions to PRE.3.b and the intent of PRE.3. 3) Train and competency-check staff; retain records. 4) Run monitoring (audits, KPIs, committee review) for scope As Applicable. 5) Collect evidence per Document expectations. 6) Track NC/CAPA to closure with evidence.', N'For PRE.3.b under PRE.3, maintain retrievable evidence suitable for Document review: controlled policies/procedures; approvals; registers; completed forms; patient/staff records; meeting minutes; improvement plans. Also retain metadata for traceability (version, author, date). NABH 6th Edition surveys may use structured evidence including app-based or photographic artefacts where the methodology permits.', N'OE PRE.3.b (Objective Element B) - parent PRE.3
- Mapped to chapter PRE: Patient Rights and Education (PRE).
- Owner: Quality Manager; departments: Quality / Patient Relations.
- Current policy/SOP and training records available.
- Operational records / sampling for As Applicable.
- Evidence pack for Document ready.
- KPIs/committees reviewed; NC/CAPA closed with evidence.', N'Medium', N'High', N'NABH;6E;PRE;OE;PRE.3.b;Document;PRE.3', 1, 1);
