  'ea75bda0-b596-8447-bce1-4e9712cdf096', 'c70ae297-d290-4858-9288-521a672d914f', N'IPC.6.a: Objective Element A. Objective element a for IPC.6 requirement.', N'Within chapter Infection Prevention and Control (IPC), objective element IPC.6.a (title: Objective Element A) is a measurable checkpoint under parent requirement IPC.6. It implements: The organisation performs surveillance to capture and monitor infection prevention and control data.. Meeting this OE demonstrates structured practice for NABH 6th Edition in this domain, reduces patient-safety and operational risk in Infection Control, and provides assessable evidence for survey.', N'1) Assign accountability: Infection Control Officer with Infection Control participation. 2) Align SOPs/work instructions to IPC.6.a and the intent of IPC.6. 3) Train and competency-check staff; retain records. 4) Run monitoring (audits, KPIs, committee review) for scope As Applicable. 5) Collect evidence per Document expectations. 6) Track NC/CAPA to closure with evidence.', N'For IPC.6.a under IPC.6, maintain retrievable evidence suitable for Document review: controlled policies/procedures; approvals; registers; completed forms; patient/staff records; meeting minutes; improvement plans. Also retain metadata for traceability (version, author, date). NABH 6th Edition surveys may use structured evidence including app-based or photographic artefacts where the methodology permits.', N'OE IPC.6.a (Objective Element A) - parent IPC.6
- Mapped to chapter IPC: Infection Prevention and Control (IPC).
- Owner: Infection Control Officer; departments: Infection Control.
- Current policy/SOP and training records available.
- Operational records / sampling for As Applicable.
- Evidence pack for Document ready.
- KPIs/committees reviewed; NC/CAPA closed with evidence.', N'Low', N'Medium', N'NABH;6E;IPC;OE;IPC.6.a;Document;IPC.6', 1, 1);
