  '16d6f5a0-f069-644f-9e67-bdabc7ef17c6', 'c61b8e01-4338-4ce4-9671-587a80643ee4', N'AAC.11.a: Objective Element A. Objective element a for AAC.11 requirement.', N'Within chapter Access Assessment and Continuity of Care (AAC), objective element AAC.11.a (title: Objective Element A) is a measurable checkpoint under parent requirement AAC.11. It implements: The preventive and promotive health services are provided in a safe, collaborative and consistent manner.. Meeting this OE demonstrates structured practice for NABH 6th Edition in this domain, reduces patient-safety and operational risk in Front Office / Clinical, and provides assessable evidence for survey.', N'1) Assign accountability: Admission In-charge with Front Office / Clinical participation. 2) Align SOPs/work instructions to AAC.11.a and the intent of AAC.11. 3) Train and competency-check staff; retain records. 4) Run monitoring (audits, KPIs, committee review) for scope As Applicable. 5) Collect evidence per Document expectations. 6) Track NC/CAPA to closure with evidence.', N'For AAC.11.a under AAC.11, maintain retrievable evidence suitable for Document review: controlled policies/procedures; approvals; registers; completed forms; patient/staff records; meeting minutes; improvement plans. Also retain metadata for traceability (version, author, date). NABH 6th Edition surveys may use structured evidence including app-based or photographic artefacts where the methodology permits.', N'OE AAC.11.a (Objective Element A) - parent AAC.11
- Mapped to chapter AAC: Access Assessment and Continuity of Care (AAC).
- Owner: Admission In-charge; departments: Front Office / Clinical.
- Current policy/SOP and training records available.
- Operational records / sampling for As Applicable.
- Evidence pack for Document ready.
- KPIs/committees reviewed; NC/CAPA closed with evidence.', N'Low', N'Medium', N'NABH;6E;AAC;OE;AAC.11.a;Document;AAC.11', 1, 1);
