  'c979eecb-24d1-4149-8a1f-1b5375ebe961', 'cee91eb1-2111-40cb-90f1-775938c6e1a0', N'IPC.7.b: Objective Element B. Objective element b for IPC.7 requirement.', N'Within chapter Infection Prevention and Control (IPC), objective element IPC.7.b (title: Objective Element B) is a measurable checkpoint under parent requirement IPC.7. It implements: Infection prevention measures include sterilisation and / or disinfection of instruments, equipment and devices.. Meeting this OE demonstrates structured practice for NABH 6th Edition in this domain, reduces patient-safety and operational risk in Infection Control, and provides assessable evidence for survey.', N'1) Assign accountability: Infection Control Officer with Infection Control participation. 2) Align SOPs/work instructions to IPC.7.b and the intent of IPC.7. 3) Train and competency-check staff; retain records. 4) Run monitoring (audits, KPIs, committee review) for scope As Applicable. 5) Collect evidence per Document expectations. 6) Track NC/CAPA to closure with evidence.', N'For IPC.7.b under IPC.7, maintain retrievable evidence suitable for Document review: controlled policies/procedures; approvals; registers; completed forms; patient/staff records; meeting minutes; improvement plans. Also retain metadata for traceability (version, author, date). NABH 6th Edition surveys may use structured evidence including app-based or photographic artefacts where the methodology permits.', N'OE IPC.7.b (Objective Element B) - parent IPC.7
- Mapped to chapter IPC: Infection Prevention and Control (IPC).
- Owner: Infection Control Officer; departments: Infection Control.
- Current policy/SOP and training records available.
- Operational records / sampling for As Applicable.
- Evidence pack for Document ready.
- KPIs/committees reviewed; NC/CAPA closed with evidence.', N'Medium', N'High', N'NABH;6E;IPC;OE;IPC.7.b;Document;IPC.7', 1, 1);
