  '1e97e3f5-3a19-7247-bd75-336cdbb5a883', '0ca19fae-d982-4b09-af79-7a6b6dc1f021', N'IPC.3.b: Objective Element B. Objective element b for IPC.3 requirement.', N'Within chapter Infection Prevention and Control (IPC), objective element IPC.3.b (title: Objective Element B) is a measurable checkpoint under parent requirement IPC.3. It implements: The organisation implements the infection prevention and control processes in clinical areas.. Meeting this OE demonstrates structured practice for NABH 6th Edition in this domain, reduces patient-safety and operational risk in Infection Control, and provides assessable evidence for survey.', N'1) Assign accountability: Infection Control Officer with Infection Control participation. 2) Align SOPs/work instructions to IPC.3.b and the intent of IPC.3. 3) Train and competency-check staff; retain records. 4) Run monitoring (audits, KPIs, committee review) for scope As Applicable. 5) Collect evidence per Document expectations. 6) Track NC/CAPA to closure with evidence.', N'For IPC.3.b under IPC.3, maintain retrievable evidence suitable for Document review: controlled policies/procedures; approvals; registers; completed forms; patient/staff records; meeting minutes; improvement plans. Also retain metadata for traceability (version, author, date). NABH 6th Edition surveys may use structured evidence including app-based or photographic artefacts where the methodology permits.', N'OE IPC.3.b (Objective Element B) - parent IPC.3
- Mapped to chapter IPC: Infection Prevention and Control (IPC).
- Owner: Infection Control Officer; departments: Infection Control.
- Current policy/SOP and training records available.
- Operational records / sampling for As Applicable.
- Evidence pack for Document ready.
- KPIs/committees reviewed; NC/CAPA closed with evidence.', N'Medium', N'High', N'NABH;6E;IPC;OE;IPC.3.b;Document;IPC.3', 1, 1);
