  '855db2fb-4c8b-ae49-84d7-a767eb888e31', '33f98f9b-8d64-4440-8a71-80eaad3289e5', N'IPC.1.d: Objective Element D. Objective element d for IPC.1 requirement.', N'Within chapter Infection Prevention and Control (IPC), objective element IPC.1.d (title: Objective Element D) is a measurable checkpoint under parent requirement IPC.1. It implements: The organisation has a comprehensive and coordinated Infection Prevention and Control (IPC) programme aimed at reducing / eliminating risks to patients, visitors, providers of care and community.. Meeting this OE demonstrates structured practice for NABH 6th Edition in this domain, reduces patient-safety and operational risk in Infection Control, and provides assessable evidence for survey.', N'1) Assign accountability: Infection Control Officer with Infection Control participation. 2) Align SOPs/work instructions to IPC.1.d and the intent of IPC.1. 3) Train and competency-check staff; retain records. 4) Run monitoring (audits, KPIs, committee review) for scope As Applicable. 5) Collect evidence per Document expectations. 6) Track NC/CAPA to closure with evidence.', N'For IPC.1.d under IPC.1, maintain retrievable evidence suitable for Document review: controlled policies/procedures; approvals; registers; completed forms; patient/staff records; meeting minutes; improvement plans. Also retain metadata for traceability (version, author, date). NABH 6th Edition surveys may use structured evidence including app-based or photographic artefacts where the methodology permits.', N'OE IPC.1.d (Objective Element D) - parent IPC.1
- Mapped to chapter IPC: Infection Prevention and Control (IPC).
- Owner: Infection Control Officer; departments: Infection Control.
- Current policy/SOP and training records available.
- Operational records / sampling for As Applicable.
- Evidence pack for Document ready.
- KPIs/committees reviewed; NC/CAPA closed with evidence.', N'Medium', N'High', N'NABH;6E;IPC;OE;IPC.1.d;Document;IPC.1', 1, 1);
