  'a88741b3-0629-8e46-a81d-c1ae29ee89a8', '7a982168-9d18-486d-a499-8844bfd561f3', N'COP.1.b: Objective Element B. Objective element b for COP.1 requirement.', N'Within chapter Care of Patients (COP), objective element COP.1.b (title: Objective Element B) is a measurable checkpoint under parent requirement COP.1. It implements: Uniform care to patients is provided in all settings of the organisation and is guided by written guidance.. Meeting this OE demonstrates structured practice for NABH 6th Edition in this domain, reduces patient-safety and operational risk in Clinical / Nursing, and provides assessable evidence for survey.', N'1) Assign accountability: Chief Medical Officer with Clinical / Nursing participation. 2) Align SOPs/work instructions to COP.1.b and the intent of COP.1. 3) Train and competency-check staff; retain records. 4) Run monitoring (audits, KPIs, committee review) for scope As Applicable. 5) Collect evidence per Document expectations. 6) Track NC/CAPA to closure with evidence.', N'For COP.1.b under COP.1, maintain retrievable evidence suitable for Document review: controlled policies/procedures; approvals; registers; completed forms; patient/staff records; meeting minutes; improvement plans. Also retain metadata for traceability (version, author, date). NABH 6th Edition surveys may use structured evidence including app-based or photographic artefacts where the methodology permits.', N'OE COP.1.b (Objective Element B) - parent COP.1
- Mapped to chapter COP: Care of Patients (COP).
- Owner: Chief Medical Officer; departments: Clinical / Nursing.
- Current policy/SOP and training records available.
- Operational records / sampling for As Applicable.
- Evidence pack for Document ready.
- KPIs/committees reviewed; NC/CAPA closed with evidence.', N'Medium', N'High', N'NABH;6E;COP;OE;COP.1.b;Document;COP.1', 1, 1);
