  '4adb3c32-6ed9-1d4d-9147-504ff163952a', '51f7aaa5-0824-46ff-a4be-8e05281fa87d', N'COP.7.a: Objective Element A. Objective element a for COP.7 requirement.', N'Within chapter Care of Patients (COP), objective element COP.7.a (title: Objective Element A) is a measurable checkpoint under parent requirement COP.7. It implements: Clinical procedures are performed in a safe manner.. Meeting this OE demonstrates structured practice for NABH 6th Edition in this domain, reduces patient-safety and operational risk in Clinical / Nursing, and provides assessable evidence for survey.', N'1) Assign accountability: Chief Medical Officer with Clinical / Nursing participation. 2) Align SOPs/work instructions to COP.7.a and the intent of COP.7. 3) Train and competency-check staff; retain records. 4) Run monitoring (audits, KPIs, committee review) for scope As Applicable. 5) Collect evidence per Document expectations. 6) Track NC/CAPA to closure with evidence.', N'For COP.7.a under COP.7, maintain retrievable evidence suitable for Document review: controlled policies/procedures; approvals; registers; completed forms; patient/staff records; meeting minutes; improvement plans. Also retain metadata for traceability (version, author, date). NABH 6th Edition surveys may use structured evidence including app-based or photographic artefacts where the methodology permits.', N'OE COP.7.a (Objective Element A) - parent COP.7
- Mapped to chapter COP: Care of Patients (COP).
- Owner: Chief Medical Officer; departments: Clinical / Nursing.
- Current policy/SOP and training records available.
- Operational records / sampling for As Applicable.
- Evidence pack for Document ready.
- KPIs/committees reviewed; NC/CAPA closed with evidence.', N'Low', N'Medium', N'NABH;6E;COP;OE;COP.7.a;Document;COP.7', 1, 1);
