  'ad4ec9c0-b517-9048-9eb9-eb4bc08b4d9e', 'f077247a-39a1-428a-a730-91050b901d84', N'IPC.2.c: Objective Element C. Objective element c for IPC.2 requirement.', N'Within chapter Infection Prevention and Control (IPC), objective element IPC.2.c (title: Objective Element C) is a measurable checkpoint under parent requirement IPC.2. It implements: The organisation provides adequate and appropriate resources for infection prevention and control.. Meeting this OE demonstrates structured practice for NABH 6th Edition in this domain, reduces patient-safety and operational risk in Infection Control, and provides assessable evidence for survey.', N'1) Assign accountability: Infection Control Officer with Infection Control participation. 2) Align SOPs/work instructions to IPC.2.c and the intent of IPC.2. 3) Train and competency-check staff; retain records. 4) Run monitoring (audits, KPIs, committee review) for scope As Applicable. 5) Collect evidence per Document expectations. 6) Track NC/CAPA to closure with evidence.', N'For IPC.2.c under IPC.2, maintain retrievable evidence suitable for Document review: controlled policies/procedures; approvals; registers; completed forms; patient/staff records; meeting minutes; improvement plans. Also retain metadata for traceability (version, author, date). NABH 6th Edition surveys may use structured evidence including app-based or photographic artefacts where the methodology permits.', N'OE IPC.2.c (Objective Element C) - parent IPC.2
- Mapped to chapter IPC: Infection Prevention and Control (IPC).
- Owner: Infection Control Officer; departments: Infection Control.
- Current policy/SOP and training records available.
- Operational records / sampling for As Applicable.
- Evidence pack for Document ready.
- KPIs/committees reviewed; NC/CAPA closed with evidence.', N'Medium', N'High', N'NABH;6E;IPC;OE;IPC.2.c;Document;IPC.2', 1, 1);
