  'a3f88e40-d021-254a-9301-5e1ec642650c', '44de507e-db15-4966-a040-98fc6318f80e', N'ROM.6.e: Objective Element E. Objective element e for ROM.6 requirement.', N'Within chapter Responsibility of Management (ROM), objective element ROM.6.e (title: Objective Element E) is a measurable checkpoint under parent requirement ROM.6. It implements: Management ensures that patient-safety aspects and risk-management issues are an integral part of patient care and hospital management.. Meeting this OE demonstrates structured practice for NABH 6th Edition in this domain, reduces patient-safety and operational risk in Management, and provides assessable evidence for survey.', N'1) Assign accountability: Administrator with Management participation. 2) Align SOPs/work instructions to ROM.6.e and the intent of ROM.6. 3) Train and competency-check staff; retain records. 4) Run monitoring (audits, KPIs, committee review) for scope As Applicable. 5) Collect evidence per Document expectations. 6) Track NC/CAPA to closure with evidence.', N'For ROM.6.e under ROM.6, maintain retrievable evidence suitable for Document review: controlled policies/procedures; approvals; registers; completed forms; patient/staff records; meeting minutes; improvement plans. Also retain metadata for traceability (version, author, date). NABH 6th Edition surveys may use structured evidence including app-based or photographic artefacts where the methodology permits.', N'OE ROM.6.e (Objective Element E) - parent ROM.6
- Mapped to chapter ROM: Responsibility of Management (ROM).
- Owner: Administrator; departments: Management.
- Current policy/SOP and training records available.
- Operational records / sampling for As Applicable.
- Evidence pack for Document ready.
- KPIs/committees reviewed; NC/CAPA closed with evidence.', N'Medium', N'High', N'NABH;6E;ROM;OE;ROM.6.e;Document;ROM.6', 1, 1);
