  '785d2139-1f89-ee4e-aae0-dafe06a7f92f', '2512dc28-6c5a-4835-84a5-9f9ad64b0032', N'FMS.1.d: Objective Element D. Objective element d for FMS.1 requirement.', N'Within chapter Facility Management and Safety (FMS), objective element FMS.1.d (title: Objective Element D) is a measurable checkpoint under parent requirement FMS.1. It implements: The organisation has a system in place to provide a safe and secure environment.. Meeting this OE demonstrates structured practice for NABH 6th Edition in this domain, reduces patient-safety and operational risk in Facility / Engineering, and provides assessable evidence for survey.', N'1) Assign accountability: Facility Manager with Facility / Engineering participation. 2) Align SOPs/work instructions to FMS.1.d and the intent of FMS.1. 3) Train and competency-check staff; retain records. 4) Run monitoring (audits, KPIs, committee review) for scope As Applicable. 5) Collect evidence per Document expectations. 6) Track NC/CAPA to closure with evidence.', N'For FMS.1.d under FMS.1, maintain retrievable evidence suitable for Document review: controlled policies/procedures; approvals; registers; completed forms; patient/staff records; meeting minutes; improvement plans. Also retain metadata for traceability (version, author, date). NABH 6th Edition surveys may use structured evidence including app-based or photographic artefacts where the methodology permits.', N'OE FMS.1.d (Objective Element D) - parent FMS.1
- Mapped to chapter FMS: Facility Management and Safety (FMS).
- Owner: Facility Manager; departments: Facility / Engineering.
- Current policy/SOP and training records available.
- Operational records / sampling for As Applicable.
- Evidence pack for Document ready.
- KPIs/committees reviewed; NC/CAPA closed with evidence.', N'Medium', N'High', N'NABH;6E;FMS;OE;FMS.1.d;Document;FMS.1', 1, 1);
