  'b25e70b6-cc07-b149-bb07-a0a6002a3f5c', '03c219a8-2336-4a9d-80d7-a9fc626f1f18', N'IMS.6.a: Objective Element A. Objective element a for IMS.6 requirement.', N'Within chapter Information Management System (IMS), objective element IMS.6.a (title: Objective Element A) is a measurable checkpoint under parent requirement IMS.6. It implements: The organisation ensures availability of current and relevant documents, records, data and information and provide for retention of the same.. Meeting this OE demonstrates structured practice for NABH 6th Edition in this domain, reduces patient-safety and operational risk in IT / Medical Records, and provides assessable evidence for survey.', N'1) Assign accountability: IT Manager with IT / Medical Records participation. 2) Align SOPs/work instructions to IMS.6.a and the intent of IMS.6. 3) Train and competency-check staff; retain records. 4) Run monitoring (audits, KPIs, committee review) for scope As Applicable. 5) Collect evidence per Document expectations. 6) Track NC/CAPA to closure with evidence.', N'For IMS.6.a under IMS.6, maintain retrievable evidence suitable for Document review: controlled policies/procedures; approvals; registers; completed forms; patient/staff records; meeting minutes; improvement plans. Also retain metadata for traceability (version, author, date). NABH 6th Edition surveys may use structured evidence including app-based or photographic artefacts where the methodology permits.', N'OE IMS.6.a (Objective Element A) - parent IMS.6
- Mapped to chapter IMS: Information Management System (IMS).
- Owner: IT Manager; departments: IT / Medical Records.
- Current policy/SOP and training records available.
- Operational records / sampling for As Applicable.
- Evidence pack for Document ready.
- KPIs/committees reviewed; NC/CAPA closed with evidence.', N'Low', N'Medium', N'NABH;6E;IMS;OE;IMS.6.a;Document;IMS.6', 1, 1);
