  '4b84882a-91dd-4447-9c56-db66eaa1471c', '1780c534-16d2-4e2b-8167-b30aee95f2a1', N'COP.7.c: Objective Element C. Objective element c for COP.7 requirement.', N'Within chapter Care of Patients (COP), objective element COP.7.c (title: Objective Element C) is a measurable checkpoint under parent requirement COP.7. It implements: Clinical procedures are performed in a safe manner.. Meeting this OE demonstrates structured practice for NABH 6th Edition in this domain, reduces patient-safety and operational risk in Clinical / Nursing, and provides assessable evidence for survey.', N'1) Assign accountability: Chief Medical Officer with Clinical / Nursing participation. 2) Align SOPs/work instructions to COP.7.c and the intent of COP.7. 3) Train and competency-check staff; retain records. 4) Run monitoring (audits, KPIs, committee review) for scope As Applicable. 5) Collect evidence per Document expectations. 6) Track NC/CAPA to closure with evidence.', N'For COP.7.c under COP.7, maintain retrievable evidence suitable for Document review: controlled policies/procedures; approvals; registers; completed forms; patient/staff records; meeting minutes; improvement plans. Also retain metadata for traceability (version, author, date). NABH 6th Edition surveys may use structured evidence including app-based or photographic artefacts where the methodology permits.', N'OE COP.7.c (Objective Element C) - parent COP.7
- Mapped to chapter COP: Care of Patients (COP).
- Owner: Chief Medical Officer; departments: Clinical / Nursing.
- Current policy/SOP and training records available.
- Operational records / sampling for As Applicable.
- Evidence pack for Document ready.
- KPIs/committees reviewed; NC/CAPA closed with evidence.', N'Medium', N'High', N'NABH;6E;COP;OE;COP.7.c;Document;COP.7', 1, 1);
