  'c953067b-978b-f54d-b7e1-56922a5b6288', '6187c94b-8eb2-4dac-825e-d1a2105793c3', N'ROM.4.a: Objective Element A. Objective element a for ROM.4 requirement.', N'Within chapter Responsibility of Management (ROM), objective element ROM.4.a (title: Objective Element A) is a measurable checkpoint under parent requirement ROM.4. It implements: The organisation is headed by a leader who shall be responsible for operating the organisation on a day-to-day basis.. Meeting this OE demonstrates structured practice for NABH 6th Edition in this domain, reduces patient-safety and operational risk in Management, and provides assessable evidence for survey.', N'1) Assign accountability: Administrator with Management participation. 2) Align SOPs/work instructions to ROM.4.a and the intent of ROM.4. 3) Train and competency-check staff; retain records. 4) Run monitoring (audits, KPIs, committee review) for scope As Applicable. 5) Collect evidence per Document expectations. 6) Track NC/CAPA to closure with evidence.', N'For ROM.4.a under ROM.4, maintain retrievable evidence suitable for Document review: controlled policies/procedures; approvals; registers; completed forms; patient/staff records; meeting minutes; improvement plans. Also retain metadata for traceability (version, author, date). NABH 6th Edition surveys may use structured evidence including app-based or photographic artefacts where the methodology permits.', N'OE ROM.4.a (Objective Element A) - parent ROM.4
- Mapped to chapter ROM: Responsibility of Management (ROM).
- Owner: Administrator; departments: Management.
- Current policy/SOP and training records available.
- Operational records / sampling for As Applicable.
- Evidence pack for Document ready.
- KPIs/committees reviewed; NC/CAPA closed with evidence.', N'Low', N'Medium', N'NABH;6E;ROM;OE;ROM.4.a;Document;ROM.4', 1, 1);
