  'fce8885b-fee0-fe49-a57d-5dd1968a33df', '453116d2-9ffb-4c85-b066-dec3e0de68fc', N'MOM.1.a: Objective Element A. Objective element a for MOM.1 requirement.', N'Within chapter Management of Medication (MOM), objective element MOM.1.a (title: Objective Element A) is a measurable checkpoint under parent requirement MOM.1. It implements: Pharmacy services and medication management is done safely.. Meeting this OE demonstrates structured practice for NABH 6th Edition in this domain, reduces patient-safety and operational risk in Pharmacy, and provides assessable evidence for survey.', N'1) Assign accountability: Chief Pharmacist with Pharmacy participation. 2) Align SOPs/work instructions to MOM.1.a and the intent of MOM.1. 3) Train and competency-check staff; retain records. 4) Run monitoring (audits, KPIs, committee review) for scope As Applicable. 5) Collect evidence per Document expectations. 6) Track NC/CAPA to closure with evidence.', N'For MOM.1.a under MOM.1, maintain retrievable evidence suitable for Document review: controlled policies/procedures; approvals; registers; completed forms; patient/staff records; meeting minutes; improvement plans. Also retain metadata for traceability (version, author, date). NABH 6th Edition surveys may use structured evidence including app-based or photographic artefacts where the methodology permits.', N'OE MOM.1.a (Objective Element A) - parent MOM.1
- Mapped to chapter MOM: Management of Medication (MOM).
- Owner: Chief Pharmacist; departments: Pharmacy.
- Current policy/SOP and training records available.
- Operational records / sampling for As Applicable.
- Evidence pack for Document ready.
- KPIs/committees reviewed; NC/CAPA closed with evidence.', N'Low', N'Medium', N'NABH;6E;MOM;OE;MOM.1.a;Document;MOM.1', 1, 1);
