  'd6d52f0a-7d01-6e4c-bb3c-721744d4734d', 'fc1b7140-ad10-4147-b9f3-e35b32f4c9d8', N'IMS.2.a: Objective Element A. Objective element a for IMS.2 requirement.', N'Within chapter Information Management System (IMS), objective element IMS.2.a (title: Objective Element A) is a measurable checkpoint under parent requirement IMS.2. It implements: The organisation has processes in place for management and control of data and information.. Meeting this OE demonstrates structured practice for NABH 6th Edition in this domain, reduces patient-safety and operational risk in IT / Medical Records, and provides assessable evidence for survey.', N'1) Assign accountability: IT Manager with IT / Medical Records participation. 2) Align SOPs/work instructions to IMS.2.a and the intent of IMS.2. 3) Train and competency-check staff; retain records. 4) Run monitoring (audits, KPIs, committee review) for scope As Applicable. 5) Collect evidence per Document expectations. 6) Track NC/CAPA to closure with evidence.', N'For IMS.2.a under IMS.2, maintain retrievable evidence suitable for Document review: controlled policies/procedures; approvals; registers; completed forms; patient/staff records; meeting minutes; improvement plans. Also retain metadata for traceability (version, author, date). NABH 6th Edition surveys may use structured evidence including app-based or photographic artefacts where the methodology permits.', N'OE IMS.2.a (Objective Element A) - parent IMS.2
- Mapped to chapter IMS: Information Management System (IMS).
- Owner: IT Manager; departments: IT / Medical Records.
- Current policy/SOP and training records available.
- Operational records / sampling for As Applicable.
- Evidence pack for Document ready.
- KPIs/committees reviewed; NC/CAPA closed with evidence.', N'Low', N'Medium', N'NABH;6E;IMS;OE;IMS.2.a;Document;IMS.2', 1, 1);
