  '6b7e58e7-c97a-e94f-9ebf-18413db3ad64', '5cd2b68f-be88-42ff-b36d-eaebb693b249', N'PSQ.3.a: Objective Element A. Objective element a for PSQ.3 requirement.', N'Within chapter Patient Safety and Quality Improvement (PSQ), objective element PSQ.3.a (title: Objective Element A) is a measurable checkpoint under parent requirement PSQ.3. It implements: The organisation identi?es key indicators to monitor the structures, processes and outcomes, which are used as tools for continual improvement.. Meeting this OE demonstrates structured practice for NABH 6th Edition in this domain, reduces patient-safety and operational risk in Quality Management, and provides assessable evidence for survey.', N'1) Assign accountability: Quality Head with Quality Management participation. 2) Align SOPs/work instructions to PSQ.3.a and the intent of PSQ.3. 3) Train and competency-check staff; retain records. 4) Run monitoring (audits, KPIs, committee review) for scope As Applicable. 5) Collect evidence per Document expectations. 6) Track NC/CAPA to closure with evidence.', N'For PSQ.3.a under PSQ.3, maintain retrievable evidence suitable for Document review: controlled policies/procedures; approvals; registers; completed forms; patient/staff records; meeting minutes; improvement plans. Also retain metadata for traceability (version, author, date). NABH 6th Edition surveys may use structured evidence including app-based or photographic artefacts where the methodology permits.', N'OE PSQ.3.a (Objective Element A) - parent PSQ.3
- Mapped to chapter PSQ: Patient Safety and Quality Improvement (PSQ).
- Owner: Quality Head; departments: Quality Management.
- Current policy/SOP and training records available.
- Operational records / sampling for As Applicable.
- Evidence pack for Document ready.
- KPIs/committees reviewed; NC/CAPA closed with evidence.', N'Low', N'Medium', N'NABH;6E;PSQ;OE;PSQ.3.a;Document;PSQ.3', 1, 1);
