  'e40a1e58-ca2c-f142-b47e-665703f9fee3', '2e5a481c-7be3-4f32-9d61-f04b0af006c9', N'HRM.12.a: Objective Element A. Objective element a for HRM.12 requirement.', N'Within chapter Human Resource Management (HRM), objective element HRM.12.a (title: Objective Element A) is a measurable checkpoint under parent requirement HRM.12. It implements: There is a process for credentialing and privileging of nursing professionals, permitted to provide patient care without supervision.. Meeting this OE demonstrates structured practice for NABH 6th Edition in this domain, reduces patient-safety and operational risk in Human Resources, and provides assessable evidence for survey.', N'1) Assign accountability: HR Manager with Human Resources participation. 2) Align SOPs/work instructions to HRM.12.a and the intent of HRM.12. 3) Train and competency-check staff; retain records. 4) Run monitoring (audits, KPIs, committee review) for scope As Applicable. 5) Collect evidence per Document expectations. 6) Track NC/CAPA to closure with evidence.', N'For HRM.12.a under HRM.12, maintain retrievable evidence suitable for Document review: controlled policies/procedures; approvals; registers; completed forms; patient/staff records; meeting minutes; improvement plans. Also retain metadata for traceability (version, author, date). NABH 6th Edition surveys may use structured evidence including app-based or photographic artefacts where the methodology permits.', N'OE HRM.12.a (Objective Element A) - parent HRM.12
- Mapped to chapter HRM: Human Resource Management (HRM).
- Owner: HR Manager; departments: Human Resources.
- Current policy/SOP and training records available.
- Operational records / sampling for As Applicable.
- Evidence pack for Document ready.
- KPIs/committees reviewed; NC/CAPA closed with evidence.', N'Low', N'Medium', N'NABH;6E;HRM;OE;HRM.12.a;Document;HRM.12', 1, 1);
